      {
        "h_title": "Method",
        "main_title": "Nam chub (Thai shrimp paste relish)",
        "author": "Luke Farrell",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Pound the shrimp paste with the salt, garlic, coriander root and chillies in a pestle and mortar. Then, add the palm sugar and pound again",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "2 tbsp of shrimp paste",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "1 tbsp of palm sugar",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Add the lime juice and warm water to combine. It should be hot, sour and salty",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "2 tbsp of warm water",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Enjoy, stirred through hot rice and with a selection of herbs and vegetables. Cucumber, celery, iceberg lettuce, radishes, Thai eggplant slices, long beans, green mango and sprigs of curry leaf all work well",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Chef Luke Farrell introduces Londoners to the lesser-known herbs, roots and pastes of southern Thailand, using plants which are grown in his tropical greenhouses in Dorset at his restaurants Speedboat Bar and Plaza Khao Gaeng.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
